  "headline_findings": {
    "te": "Direct whole-player Ridge feature families did not stably beat validated v0.4 on 2020-2024; keep validated v0.4 TE as control while target-specific research continues.",
    "rookies": "NFL draft capital strongly improves rookie year-1 forecasts over a simple prior-cohort position mean across 2018-2024 for QB/RB/WR/TE.",
    "young_players": "Validated v0.4 under-projects first-year-history RB/WR and year-1/year-2 TE on average; upstream projection bias remains relevant to the separate dynasty audit.",
    "role_survival": "Chronological logistic role-survival models beat simple prior-role persistence in all evaluated folds for QB/RB/WR/TE.",
    "availability": "Simple expected-games x per-game decomposition is unstable and is rejected as a universal replacement.",
    "uncertainty": "Rolling empirical whole-player 80% intervals are approximately calibrated but wide; history-conditioned calibration helps some positions but not all.",
    "breakouts": "Breakout events are only weakly predictable and do not justify a breakout model.",
    "collapses": "Collapse risk is materially more predictable than breakout risk and is more promising as an uncertainty/risk feature than as a point-forecast override."
  },
